#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:77
msgid ""
"You should now notice that your turtle is driving around uncontrollably like "
"in this screenshot. Let's try to understand reason behind that behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:80
msgid ""
"In our code we asked tf2 the following question: \"What was the pose of "
"``carrot1`` 5 seconds ago, relative to ``turtle2`` 5 seconds ago?\". This "
"means we are controlling the second turtle based on where it was 5 seconds "
"ago as well as where the first carrot was 5 seconds ago."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:83
msgid ""
"However, what we really want to ask is: \"What was the pose of ``carrot1`` 5 "
"seconds ago, relative to the current position of the ``turtle2``?\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:86
msgid "Advanced API for lookupTransform()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:88
msgid ""
"To ask the tf2 that particular question, we will use an advanced API that "
"gives us the power to say explicitly when to acquire the specified "
"transformations. This is done by calling the ``lookupTransform()`` method "
"with additional parameters. Your code now would look like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:92
msgid ""
"rclcpp::Time now = this->get_clock()->now();\n"
"rclcpp::Time when = now - rclcpp::Duration(5, 0);\n"
"try {\n"
"    t = tf_buffer_->lookupTransform(\n"
"        toFrameRel,\n"
"        now,\n"
"        fromFrameRel,\n"
"        when,\n"
"        \"world\",\n"
"        50ms);\n"
"} catch (const tf2::TransformException & ex) {"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:106
msgid "The advanced API for ``lookupTransform()`` takes six arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:108
msgid "Target frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:110
msgid "The time to transform to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:112
msgid "Source frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:114
msgid "The time at which source frame will be evaluated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:116
msgid "Frame that does not change over time, in this case the ``world`` frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:118
msgid "Time to wait for the target frame to become available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:120
msgid ""
"To sum up, tf2 does the following in the background. In the past, it "
"computes the transform from the ``carrot1`` to the ``world``. In the "
"``world`` frame, tf2 time travels from the past to now. And at the current "
"time, tf2 computes the transform from the ``world`` to the ``turtle2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:126
msgid "Checking the results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:128
msgid ""
"Build the package then let's run the simulation again, this time with the "
"advanced time-travel API:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:152
msgid ""
"And yes, the second turtle is directed to where the first carrot was 5 "
"seconds ago!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:155
msgid "Summary"
msgstr "摘要"

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Time-Travel-With-Tf2-Cpp.rst:157
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, you have seen one of the advanced features of tf2. You "
"learned that tf2 can transform data in time and learned how to do that with "
"turtlesim example. tf2 allowed you to go back in time and make frame "
"transformations between old and current poses of turtles by using the "
"advanced ``lookupTransform()`` API."
msgstr ""
